From: Mary (mary-ext/crossover-wine-endfield)
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Cache the window under the cursor.

For every mouse-moved event, winemac asks WindowServer which window is under
the cursor with windowNumberAtPoint:, a synchronous query. When a game holds
the cursor still for mouse-look, every event asks about the same point; with a
1000 Hz mouse this was a noticeable part of the main thread's CPU. Reuse the
answer for 50 ms while the point is unchanged.

Source: https://github.com/mary-ext/crossover-wine-endfield
        patches/wine/macos/0013-winemac-cache-the-window-under-the-cursor.patch
        at commit 3ac05a11 (2026-10-17), rebased onto Wine 11.19 (code unchanged).
License: Wine LGPL-2.1-or-later.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
index 03d98a8..3961732 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -1345,9 +1345,23 @@ - (void) handleMouseMove:(NSEvent*)anEvent
             CGPoint cgpoint = CGEventGetLocation([anEvent CGEvent]);
             NSPoint point = [self flippedMouseLocation:NSPointFromCGPoint(cgpoint)];
             NSInteger windowUnderNumber;
-
-            windowUnderNumber = [NSWindow windowNumberAtPoint:point
-                                  belowWindowWithWindowNumber:0];
+            /* Avoid repeated synchronous WindowServer queries while the cursor is pinned.
+               Cache accessed only on the main thread. */
+            static NSPoint cachedPoint;
+            static NSInteger cachedWindowNumber;
+            static NSTimeInterval cachedTime;
+            NSTimeInterval now = [anEvent timestamp];
+
+            if (NSEqualPoints(point, cachedPoint) && now - cachedTime < 0.05 && now >= cachedTime)
+                windowUnderNumber = cachedWindowNumber;
+            else
+            {
+                windowUnderNumber = [NSWindow windowNumberAtPoint:point
+                                      belowWindowWithWindowNumber:0];
+                cachedPoint = point;
+                cachedWindowNumber = windowUnderNumber;
+                cachedTime = now;
+            }
             targetWindow = (WineWindow*)[NSApp windowWithWindowNumber:windowUnderNumber];
             if (!NSMouseInRect(point, [targetWindow contentRectForFrameRect:[targetWindow frame]], NO))
                 targetWindow = nil;
